        "reviewer": "Codex independent chemistry reviewer /root/chemie426_five_existing_visuals_independent",
        "reason": "Use the exact current e9 whole goal, the already reviewed unchanged corrected case-1/case-2 and rubric objects, the unchanged required aspect-1/aspect-2 expectations, and this exact corrected axis. The remaining new operator ambiguity from the prior own P2 is resolved for this exact composition.\n\nThe exact corrected e9 whole case pair and existing required aspect IDs/coverage/variation rules remain scientifically usable at E1/G1 design level. The supplied pKa values and dominant-form models are not new measurements, and this judgment establishes no learner has demonstrated them.\n\nOriginal bounded HE primary-source evidence remains pinned and unchanged. No new country/track source claim, curriculum release or fresh D role is introduced.",
        "evidenceLevel": "E1",
